          "normalized_message": "--rmi all ban misses --rmi=all form and folded variants | The global ban matches the literal substring '--rmi all' on a raw line. '--rmi=all' or '--rmi all' split across a folded block with different whitespace survives normalization only for the 'all' check (the ban scans raw lines, not the normalized run), so the equivalent long-form flag bypasses the gate. Inconsistent with the teardown check, which operates on normalized text. | Evidence: if \"--rmi all\" in line: | Fix: Apply the ban against the normaliz",
