          "normalized_message": "New ci.yml step duplicates enforcement without failing informatively on drift | The ci.yml step and the pre-commit hook invoke the same pytest module, so the six-line echo banner in ci.yml restates what the test module docstring already states. Any drift between the two invocation contexts (e.g. uv availability in pre-commit environments) yields two failure surfaces for one check. Harmless, but redundant policy prose in CI logs tends to rot. | Evidence: echo \"Per-run 'up --build' compose images must be evic",
